From 2b31205c2b988289d71643e45acdef29ff71e706 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Oct 2023 14:02:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] zsmalloc: use copy_page for full page copy

Some architectures have implemented optimized copy_page for full page
copying, such as arm.

On my arm platform, use the copy_page helper for single page copying is
about 10 percent faster than memcpy.

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20231006060245.7411-1-mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com
Signed-off-by: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>
Reviewed-by: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Cc: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
Cc: Matthias Brugger <matthias.bgg@gmail.com>
Cc: Minchan Kim <minchan@kernel.org>
Cc: YJ Chiang <yj.chiang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---
 mm/zsmalloc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/zsmalloc.c b/mm/zsmalloc.c
index 170e9b5e1..0d2abc3f3 100644
--- a/mm/zsmalloc.c
+++ b/mm/zsmalloc.c
@@ -2014,7 +2014,7 @@ static int zs_page_migrate(struct address_space *mapping, struct page *newpage,
 	 * Here, any user cannot access all objects in the zspage so let's move.
 	 */
 	d_addr = kmap_atomic(newpage);
-	memcpy(d_addr, s_addr, PAGE_SIZE);
+	copy_page(d_addr, s_addr);
 	kunmap_atomic(d_addr);
 
 	for (addr = s_addr + offset; addr < s_addr + pos;
